orts a list of integers in ascending order.\"\"\"\n    return sorted(arr)\ndef _reverse_integers(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Reverses the order of a list of integers.\"\"\"\n    return arr[::-1]\ndef _get_digit_name(num: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Retrieves the English word name for a single digit.\"\"\"\n    return _DIGIT_NAMES_MAP.get(num, \"\")\ndef _map_to_digit_names(arr: list[int]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Replaces each integer in a list with its corresponding English word name.\"\"\"\n    return [_get_digit_name(num) for num in arr]\ndef by_length(arr: list[int]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts integers between 1 and 9, reverses them, and replaces with word names.\n    Ignores numbers outside the 1-9 range.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return []\n\n    filtered_arr = _filter_valid_integers(arr)\n    sorted_arr = _sort_integers_ascending(filtered_arr)\n    reversed_arr = _reverse_integers(sorted_arr)\n    result_arr = _map_to_digit_names(reversed_arr)\n\n    return result_arr", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/100": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/100", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef make_a_pile(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, you have to make a pile of n levels of stones.\n    The first level has n stones.\n    The number of stones in the next level is:\n        - the next odd number if n is odd.\n        - the next even number if n is even.\n    Return the number of stones in each level in a list, where element at index\n    i represents the number of stones in the level (i+1).\n\n    Examples:\n    >>> make_a_pile(3)\n    [3, 5, 7]\n    \"\"\"\n    pile_of_stones: List[int] = [n]\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        previous_level_stones = pile_of_stones[i - 1]\n        current_level_stones = previous_level_stones + 2\n        pile_of_stones.append(current_level_stones)\n\n    return pile_of_stones", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pas